## Aggregate per class (mode A)

- FD_OPEN    (n=5): mean bytes delta -0.179 %  (4 wins -70/-69/-20/-31 B + 1 no-op)
- PHOTO_CTRL (n=6): mean bytes delta -0.243 %  (4 wins, 2 mild regressions on 1025469)
- PHOTO_LOWD (n=3): mean bytes delta  0.000 %  (gate already fires in baseline at d=1,2,3 for tot=4096)
- SCREEN     (n=2): mean bytes delta +0.097 %  (terminal +62 B, codec_wiki +5 B)
- WORST SSIM2 regression: 0.0000 (byte-identical decoded pixels on every cell with a delta)
- WORST bytes regression: +0.601 % on 1025469 e7 d=6

Mode B is structurally identical to A on every cell (both fire on
tot ≥ 1024 here); ignore unless re-running with tot < 1024 fixtures.

## Acceptance gate analysis (task spec)

- (a) ≥ -1 % bytes mean improvement on the residual cluster ❌
      FD_OPEN mean -0.179 % (need ≤ -1.0 %)
- (b) Zero regressions ≥ +0.5 % bytes elsewhere ❌
      1025469 e7 d=6 +0.601 % (exceeds budget by 0.10 pp)
- (c) SSIM2 within ±0.3 everywhere ✅
      Worst SSIM2 delta 0.0000 (decoded pixels are identical when
      bytes differ; the context-map rebuckets same data)
- (d) Hash-locks 36/36 BYTE-IDENTICAL ✅ (env unset = libjxl parity)
- (e) Libjxl byte-lock 4/4 BYTE-IDENTICAL ✅
- (f) Drift 7/7 PASS ✅
- (g) Lib tests 1508/1508 PASS ✅

## Honest-stop verdict

Same shape as W44-84's honest-stop. The W44-73 ANS+LZ77 context-map
writer landing did NOT meaningfully compound the wins. Reason:

The cluster-count formula `nb_clusters_luma = (tot / size_for_ctx_model
/ 2).clamp(2, 9)` uses our widened `size_for_ctx_model = 1024`.
At tot=4096: clamp(2, 2, 9) = **2 luma clusters**.
At tot=4096: `nb_clusters_chroma = clamp(0, 1, 5) = 1 chroma cluster`.

So even after widening, we emit a 3-cluster context map vs the
4-cluster default — yielding a small per-image rebucketing win when the
ANS+LZ77 writer happens to find a tighter encoding (and a small loss
when it doesn't). Net wins / losses are in the 0.1-1.0 % range per
cell, mostly cancelling out. No mechanism to lift the cluster count
without a different lever (e.g., decoupling `nb_clusters_luma` from
`size_for_ctx_model`).

The W44-84 ceiling of ~150 B per cell still holds.

## DO NOT (binding for future agents)

- DO NOT respawn this chunk with another threshold value (A, B, C,
  ½, ¼ etc). Measurement is conclusive across W44-84 + this retry that
  `tot < 1024` is the structural floor; further widening produces
  identical output on cells with tot ≥ 1024 (which is every photo /
  screenshot ≥ 256×256).
- DO NOT default-flip without addressing the cluster-count ceiling.
  Mean -0.179 % FD_OPEN win + one +0.601 % photo regression = not worth
  a hash-lock regen + bitstream change.
- DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any byte movement. The bytes differ
  because the per-image cluster MAPPING differs; decoded pixels are
  byte-identical (SSIM2 delta 0.0000 on every cell that moves).
- DO NOT widen `nb_clusters_luma` formula independently without first
  measuring the photo regression. W44-84 recommendation #2 specifically
  warned this is also "not the right lever".

## Follow-on candidates (NOT in #61 scope)

1. **DIFFERENT lever: lift `nb_clusters_luma` cap above 2 at
   tot=4096** by decoupling from `size_for_ctx_model` (e.g., minimum
   3 luma when `tot >= 4096`). MUST be measured against the W44-84
   "max -157 B per cell" ceiling first; may regress mid-tot photos.
2. **Per-image discriminator** (W44-91-style ZenanalyzeProxies) to
   admit the widening only on F-D-class content. Higher cost; would
   add another Section B row in LIBJXL_DIVERGENCES.md; not justified
   by -0.2 % wins.
3. **Address remaining ~100-700 B per F-D OPEN cell from other
   levers**: HfMetadata, AC strategy selection, quant calibration.
   Adaptive context-map widening can contribute at most ~150 B; the
   remaining 500-600 B per cell lives elsewhere (W44-84 final
   recommendation).

## Source state

`jxl-encoder/src/vardct/ac_context.rs` retains the env-var hook
(diagnostic-only, byte-identical when env unset). Mirrors the
W44-205 / W44-audit-5 pattern of preserving the AB harness for
future re-investigation.

`examples/issue_61_block_ctx_map_widen_ab.rs` registered in
`jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml` under
`required-features = ["parallel", "butteraugli-loop", "ssim2-loop", "__expert"]`.

NO production source path changed. NO hash-lock churn. NO threshold
default-flip.
